WEBVTT

00:03.753 --> 00:04.753
What happened?

00:04.754 --> 00:05.921
Is it sick?

00:05.922 --> 00:07.007
Huh?

00:07.632 --> 00:09.258
But how?

00:09.259 --> 00:11.219
It's better not to touch it.

00:12.554 --> 00:14.388
A strange dead cat?

00:14.389 --> 00:16.849
Yeah, it was pretty creepy.

00:16.850 --> 00:19.227
I've seen something like that, too.

00:19.519 --> 00:23.856
It wasn't a cat, but a strange rat
died behind our house.

00:23.857 --> 00:26.442
Is there some disease
going around, perhaps?

00:26.443 --> 00:28.318
It's possible.

00:28.319 --> 00:31.947
Everyone, make sure to wash
your hands thoroughly, okay?

00:31.948 --> 00:33.282
- Yes!
- I understand.

00:33.283 --> 00:34.701
Rudeus!

00:38.538 --> 00:40.999
Lise is pregnant.

00:42.167 --> 00:44.334
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations, Grandma!

00:44.335 --> 00:46.129
Thank you.

00:46.379 --> 00:51.258
A child, huh?
I'd like to have one with Roxy, too.

00:51.259 --> 00:53.636
I wonder what Roxy thinks about it.

00:54.095 --> 00:56.639
I'd be happy if she wanted
the same thing.

01:02.604 --> 01:04.606
What's that loud noise?

01:05.398 --> 01:07.108
Roxy!

01:10.737 --> 01:13.405
An Advanced-tier Detoxification spell
doesn't work.

01:13.406 --> 01:15.408
Do you know what illness she has?

01:17.702 --> 01:19.204
Petrification syndrome.

01:20.413 --> 01:21.414
Excuse me.

01:26.085 --> 01:30.215
Only a God-tier Detoxification spell
can treat this disease.

01:37.430 --> 01:39.640
What did you say just now?

01:39.641 --> 01:44.895
The Holy Country of Millis has scripture
on God-tier Detoxification spell.

01:44.896 --> 01:48.440
That's the only way to save Roxy.

01:48.441 --> 01:51.610
I know where they keep it.

01:51.611 --> 01:54.697
I will lead you there, Rudeus.

01:55.198 --> 01:57.492
Of course, I'll go, too.

02:00.870 --> 02:04.082
Thank you, both of you.

02:05.291 --> 02:08.711
Intruders!
They stole the holy scripture!

02:13.258 --> 02:17.637
Millis forces ambushed us
at the teleportation circle.

02:21.099 --> 02:22.892
That was the first time...

02:23.768 --> 02:25.728
I killed a human.

03:03.474 --> 03:05.851
It's been a while, Rudeus!

03:05.852 --> 03:09.230
Ghislaine and... Eris?

03:09.522 --> 03:11.523
Why is she here?

03:11.524 --> 03:14.568
You see...
I heard about you at school.

03:14.569 --> 03:17.779
You wounded a demon king,
became a top student,

03:17.780 --> 03:19.740
and even defeated the Hydra alone.

03:19.741 --> 03:24.411
I also heard you gave up your left hand
to defeat one of the Seven Great Powers...

03:24.412 --> 03:26.039
What business do you have here?

03:28.875 --> 03:30.877
I have grown stronger!

03:31.252 --> 03:34.588
I know you might already
be much stronger.

03:34.589 --> 03:37.967
Still, I've become stronger
so I could be with you!

03:38.343 --> 03:40.178
That's why...

03:40.595 --> 03:42.347
Let's get married!

03:45.391 --> 03:47.602
What are you talking about?

03:48.228 --> 03:50.354
What kind of bullshit is that?!

03:50.355 --> 03:53.149
Do you know how much
I've suffered because of you?!

03:55.068 --> 03:57.362
I already have two wives.

03:57.904 --> 03:59.697
I can't be with you.

04:06.537 --> 04:08.288
Is that really okay?

04:08.289 --> 04:09.791
Our priority now is Roxy.

04:10.250 --> 04:12.001
Why now?

04:58.548 --> 05:00.383
Roxy is gone now.

05:01.009 --> 05:02.635
That Roxy I loved...

05:12.562 --> 05:16.773
Rudy, I won't tell you to cheer up.

05:16.774 --> 05:20.945
It's about time we moved on
together, as a family.

05:21.487 --> 05:24.364
We're all grieving for Roxy.

05:24.365 --> 05:28.202
But I don't think Roxy would be happy
to see you like this.

05:33.249 --> 05:35.209
If it'll help ease your mind,

05:36.419 --> 05:39.505
you can use my body
as much as you want.

05:40.715 --> 05:43.885
There's no way I can sleep with you
when you're saying things like that!

05:46.304 --> 05:47.388
I'm sorry.

05:52.977 --> 05:58.190
If I sleep with Sylphie right now,
I'm sure I'll treat her roughly.

05:58.191 --> 06:00.442
I'd imagine she was Roxy,

06:00.443 --> 06:02.737
then use her as a punching bag
to take out my frustration.

06:16.292 --> 06:19.045
We've been seeing a lot of
each other lately.

06:19.629 --> 06:23.341
So what kind of shitty marriage proposal
do you have for me today?

06:26.719 --> 06:28.471
What's this all about?!

06:34.227 --> 06:38.564
No one understands
how I feel anyway.

06:39.482 --> 06:41.067
Come again, okay?

07:08.761 --> 07:10.179
I'll be back.

07:16.269 --> 07:18.187
Sylphie...

07:18.855 --> 07:21.399
Am I not good enough?!

07:21.858 --> 07:23.025
Sylphie!

07:26.446 --> 07:29.740
A few days later, Sylphie left home.

07:30.283 --> 07:32.701
Lilia told me to chase after her,

07:32.702 --> 07:35.580
but I didn't know if
I even had the right.

07:36.205 --> 07:39.375
If only Elinalise were here...

07:48.634 --> 07:53.930
It seems Sylphie left for the Kingdom
of Asura with Ariel and her allies.

07:53.931 --> 07:56.309
If I hurry, I should still be
able to catch up to her.

07:59.812 --> 08:01.439
I want to apologize to her,

08:01.981 --> 08:05.526
go home together,
and start over with everyone.

08:08.571 --> 08:12.532
I never thought I would have to enter
the Kingdom of Asura illegally.

08:12.533 --> 08:16.621
I'll get the carriage ready,
so stay here.

08:17.246 --> 08:19.956
I'm fine with making deals with bandits,

08:19.957 --> 08:23.794
but I'm worried Sylphie might get
the wrong idea if she sees us together.

08:29.592 --> 08:31.134
Why is she here?

08:31.135 --> 08:34.137
Wait, the Kingdom of Asura
is her homeland.

08:34.138 --> 08:36.265
It's not strange for her to be here.

08:38.851 --> 08:41.561
According to that bandit, Triss,

08:41.562 --> 08:45.482
the king of Asura is sick
and doesn't have much time left.

08:45.483 --> 08:50.737
I'm sure Ariel rushed back here
to join the struggle for the throne.

08:50.738 --> 08:53.865
Are you sure Princess Ariel
is staging a coup d'état?

08:53.866 --> 08:56.536
But it looks like she got caught.

08:56.869 --> 08:59.455
Rumor has it she'll be executed soon.

09:09.757 --> 09:11.758
You rebels!

09:11.759 --> 09:14.427
How dare you disturb
the peace of the capital!

09:14.428 --> 09:16.472
You're a disgrace!

09:33.531 --> 09:36.242
Sylphie! Sylphie!

09:38.077 --> 09:41.247
No way... Sylphie...

09:42.999 --> 09:44.791
Who the hell are you?

09:44.792 --> 09:47.420
Are you one of their comrades?!

09:54.969 --> 09:59.432
Don't you dare defile her!

10:02.810 --> 10:04.687
I don't care anymore.

10:05.021 --> 10:07.897
This country can just go to hell.

10:07.898 --> 10:10.901
Everything can just disappear.

10:25.708 --> 10:29.502
You've been nagging me
a lot today, haven't you?

10:29.503 --> 10:32.589
You're ruining my booze,
so could you please shut up?

10:32.590 --> 10:34.467
No, I won't.

10:34.842 --> 10:37.928
Every day, you get drunk
and throw money away.

10:38.512 --> 10:41.431
To top it all off, you even
brought a prostitute home.

10:41.432 --> 10:44.351
I'm the head of this household.

10:44.352 --> 10:46.978
I can do whatever I want here.

10:46.979 --> 10:50.982
If we're short on money,
you can just sell your body.

10:50.983 --> 10:54.944
If you keep this up,
it'll be bad for Lucie, too.

10:54.945 --> 10:57.697
You'll tear our household apart.

10:57.698 --> 10:59.532
"Our household"?

10:59.533 --> 11:01.993
This is my home.

11:01.994 --> 11:05.998
I made this a home where
Sylphie and I could be happy.

11:06.415 --> 11:08.958
A freeloader like you...

11:08.959 --> 11:11.962
Stop acting like my mother!
You're just a lowly maid!

12:48.309 --> 12:54.690
Why couldn't I get my act together
after losing Roxy?

13:00.821 --> 13:03.281
Big Brother, welcome back.

13:03.282 --> 13:06.202
Your food is ready.
Just give me a moment, okay?

13:10.998 --> 13:12.208
Heya!

13:12.958 --> 13:14.210
You...

13:14.793 --> 13:18.087
Even when I call you,
you never show up when it matters.

13:18.088 --> 13:20.089
What do you want from me now?

13:20.090 --> 13:22.801
I thought I'd see you one last time.

13:23.093 --> 13:25.429
One last time?
What do you mean?

13:25.721 --> 13:27.222
Exactly what I said.

13:27.223 --> 13:29.892
It means I don't need you anymore.

13:31.477 --> 13:35.231
We met after the Teleportation
Incident, right?

13:35.606 --> 13:38.066
I was really panicking back then.

13:38.067 --> 13:40.860
My future had suddenly changed,
you know.

13:40.861 --> 13:44.239
Since my blessing
doesn't work on you,

13:44.240 --> 13:47.117
it was really hard to earn your trust.

13:47.368 --> 13:51.371
But in the end,
you agreed to grant my request.

13:51.372 --> 13:53.540
All that hard work paid off!

13:53.541 --> 13:55.000
Your request?

13:55.376 --> 13:58.044
Wasn't it about checking
out the basement?

13:58.045 --> 14:02.383
That's right. And thanks to you,
I was able to kill Roxy.

14:06.428 --> 14:09.055
What are you talking about?

14:09.056 --> 14:11.517
Stop joking.
It's not funny.

14:14.937 --> 14:16.105
You...

14:16.939 --> 14:19.566
You killed Roxy?

14:19.567 --> 14:22.151
Technically, no.

14:22.152 --> 14:24.697
I can't act directly.

14:24.989 --> 14:29.368
I just gave you advice as usual,
and you followed it.

14:30.411 --> 14:33.289
In that sense,
the one who killed her...

14:34.248 --> 14:35.498
was you.

14:35.499 --> 14:37.501
So you killed her!

14:37.835 --> 14:39.378
It was you...!

14:40.963 --> 14:42.381
It was you...

14:46.552 --> 14:49.304
That look on your face!
That's exactly what I wanted to see!

14:49.305 --> 14:52.515
Why did you do that to Roxy?

14:52.516 --> 14:54.726
Things have been hell since then!

14:54.727 --> 14:57.938
Everyone... Everyone is gone!

14:58.272 --> 15:00.481
That's your problem.

15:00.482 --> 15:04.027
You always had a tendency
to end up like this.

15:04.028 --> 15:07.156
Don't blame everything on me.

15:07.698 --> 15:12.827
Well, it was fun watching you
fall apart.

15:12.828 --> 15:14.455
You bastard!

15:15.456 --> 15:19.585
Oh, I'll tell you one more thing.

15:20.044 --> 15:25.049
Roxy was pregnant.

15:26.050 --> 15:31.680
Thanks to you being such an idiot,
everything went exactly as I planned.

15:34.642 --> 15:37.353
Well then, good job.

15:39.271 --> 15:43.107
Hey! Bastard!
I'm not done with you yet!

15:43.108 --> 15:44.318
Man-God!

15:44.610 --> 15:46.320
Man-God!

16:03.295 --> 16:07.257
I wondered...
Was he just a dream?

16:07.591 --> 16:11.553
After all, I hadn't found any evidence
that he even existed.

16:12.388 --> 16:13.429
No.

16:13.430 --> 16:15.264
The feeling of his hand
on my shoulder...

16:15.265 --> 16:16.766
His laughter...

16:16.767 --> 16:18.310
Everything was real.

16:18.894 --> 16:21.437
I have to do whatever it takes
to find out more about him.

16:21.438 --> 16:22.814
I need to find him.

16:22.815 --> 16:25.859
And kill that bastard.

16:29.697 --> 16:30.698
Hey.

16:32.199 --> 16:37.121
Have you ever heard of the Man-God?

16:39.498 --> 16:41.833
This one's a bust, too.

16:41.834 --> 16:45.295
Is there anyone who might know?

16:49.174 --> 16:53.429
Hey, it's about time you told me
about the Man-God.

16:53.762 --> 16:54.888
Eris.

16:56.890 --> 16:59.268
What's with that look?!

17:06.817 --> 17:08.443
Just say something!

17:08.444 --> 17:10.738
You're not usually this quiet, are you?

17:11.363 --> 17:17.785
She's been getting in my way
ever since Sylphie died.

17:17.786 --> 17:19.912
She knows something.

17:19.913 --> 17:21.498
She has to.

17:24.543 --> 17:27.462
I want to visit Perugius
and ask about the Man-God.

17:27.463 --> 17:31.174
But it'd be dangerous
if he's on the Man-God's side.

17:31.175 --> 17:33.677
I have to proceed with caution.

17:40.768 --> 17:42.061
Mr. Greyrat?!

17:45.397 --> 17:46.398
Aisha!

17:46.648 --> 17:47.858
Aisha!

17:52.488 --> 17:53.864
Zanoba...

18:21.225 --> 18:23.643
Aisha and Zanoba
treated me the same as ever,

18:23.644 --> 18:25.604
even though I was acting like scum.

18:26.230 --> 18:30.442
Why couldn't I be by their side
when it mattered most?

18:31.193 --> 18:35.030
No, not yet.
There are still things I have to do.

18:35.489 --> 18:39.201
The long-lived, immortal demons
must know something about the Man-God.

18:39.660 --> 18:41.578
I haven't lost yet.

18:49.628 --> 18:52.589
O hero! Not bad!

18:57.928 --> 18:59.680
I can see through it!

19:03.934 --> 19:04.934
I can do this!

19:04.935 --> 19:07.312
I just have to keep
squashing her like this.

19:08.981 --> 19:10.899
Bestow upon me thy power,

19:11.275 --> 19:13.317
Water Spirits!

19:13.318 --> 19:15.195
Deep Mist!

19:19.616 --> 19:21.118
Where's Atofe?

19:21.702 --> 19:23.537
Got you!

19:29.168 --> 19:30.377
Eris?!

19:40.470 --> 19:43.640
I can't pull it out!

19:47.019 --> 19:49.188
Moore!

19:49.313 --> 19:51.648
Find them!

19:57.905 --> 20:01.158
Eris, why...?

20:02.284 --> 20:06.121
She only wanted to stand by your side.

20:07.915 --> 20:11.543
She hasn't changed since back then.

20:12.252 --> 20:15.297
She worked hard for your sake.

20:15.672 --> 20:19.801
She believed you'd one day understand
and accept her.

20:21.053 --> 20:25.056
But you've changed.

20:25.057 --> 20:26.558
No way...

20:27.142 --> 20:30.312
Then, all this time, she...

20:30.812 --> 20:36.318
She always...
She always loved me?

20:37.694 --> 20:42.199
How was I supposed to know?

20:52.000 --> 20:55.337
And now, there's no one left.

20:55.879 --> 20:58.298
I couldn't protect any of them.

20:59.049 --> 21:00.801
It's all the Man-God's fault.

21:01.176 --> 21:05.347
I'll kill the Man-God
if it's the last thing I do.

21:08.892 --> 21:12.062
Finally... I finally found it!

21:12.437 --> 21:16.941
This world was originally
made up of six worlds,

21:16.942 --> 21:19.318
arranged like six faces,

21:19.319 --> 21:22.572
just like a six-sided die.

21:23.156 --> 21:28.452
That Man-God is in a world called the
Barren World, which lies at the center.

21:28.453 --> 21:31.748
It seems you can get there
using the Dragonfolk's secret art.

21:32.332 --> 21:37.212
But what are these five sacred
treasures needed to use it?

21:39.798 --> 21:46.137
According to Perugius, all five treasures
would appear within a few decades.

21:46.138 --> 21:49.933
But I don't think I'll live that long.

21:50.851 --> 21:53.145
I'm tired now.

21:53.729 --> 21:57.815
Even my resentment toward
the Man-God is starting to fade.

21:57.816 --> 22:02.029
Why have I been doing this,
and for whose sake?

22:11.747 --> 22:13.289
I'll go back to the past.

22:13.290 --> 22:17.084
Summoning magic and the magic
described on the Dragonfolk murals...

22:17.085 --> 22:20.046
If I combine them
and adjust the method,

22:20.047 --> 22:22.257
it might be possible
to travel to the past.

22:25.218 --> 22:27.678
But I have a lot of concerns.

22:27.679 --> 22:32.016
Would my past self believe me?

22:32.017 --> 22:34.770
I'm not even sure this will work
in the first place.

22:36.980 --> 22:39.940
But if it works,

22:39.941 --> 22:43.111
I might be able to give the Man-God
a taste of his own medicine.

22:48.742 --> 22:52.620
Sorry. You've done enough.
You don't have to say any more.

22:52.621 --> 22:56.500
I don't want you to have any regrets...

22:57.459 --> 23:01.921
About the basement, Nanahoshi, Eris...

23:01.922 --> 23:04.174
And about the Man-God.

23:04.966 --> 23:07.636
Did I manage to get my point across?

23:08.637 --> 23:12.891
At least let me see Sylphie and Roxy,
even just once...

23:16.770 --> 23:21.399
Oh! Sylphie... Roxy...

23:21.983 --> 23:24.402
Damn it...

23:24.945 --> 23:30.450
You two are as adorable as ever...

23:32.911 --> 23:35.913
(Episode 13)
(Diary)

23:35.914 --> 23:40.919
(Next Episode)
(Resolve)
